Z||000000||extinct||11-12-2001||10:52 PM||||My 35K formula appears to be leaking a small amount of brake fluid from the bolt that holds the e-brake mechanism to the rear drivers side caliper. <P>1. Can that seal be replaced by itself?<BR>2. if not do I buy a rebuilt gm caliper?<BR>3. or can I go to any parts store and order<BR>   a new or rebuilt caliper?<BR>4. Finally, If I replace/fix the caliper, do<BR>   I also have to replace the other side too?<P>Thanks...||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-12-2001||11:36 PM||||The seal is quit. the question is why. That's what will determin if it's easily rebuildable.<P>The first issue... do the bleeders open? If not then you've got more issues. <P>If the actuator screw or hole are damaged, you may have to replace the caliper.<P>Never, Never, Never, spray the actuators with oil/grease.... That will trash the seal as well. If that's the case here, then the caliper can probably be saved with a rebuild kit. (As opposed to oil inside the caliper which would likely damage things beyond easy DIY repair.)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||extinct||11-12-2001||11:45 PM||||The bleeders do open.  A month ago I bled the brakes using valvoline syntec dot 3/4. The fluid that was in there actually looked good.  So if its just the one seal, can it be replaced by itseld, and will the whole caliper have to come off to do it?<P>Thanks for you help!!||||reg||1
